{"title":"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the figure, the area of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b076f2e7f124fc5d8b5ef7b30b95bfcfe85449f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WXYZ$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/4/8c401da100e4ee9c4132a90cf9f6a74e90efbab2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25 \\text{ cm}^2$\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />. The four smaller squares have sides 1 cm long, either parallel to or coinciding with the sides of the large square. In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/a/f3ac37c9fa391eebb9601bfaca8bfbfaabdf5ca1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = AC$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />, and when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is folded over side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> coincides with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, the center of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b076f2e7f124fc5d8b5ef7b30b95bfcfe85449f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WXYZ$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" />. What is the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, in square centimeters?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/5/fb5de36e57bfb81488edf36e2717cf7b93f0444b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(fontsize(8)); size(225); pair Z=origin, W=(0,10), X=(10,10), Y=(10,0), O=(5,5), B=(-4,8), C=(-4,2), A=(-13,5); draw((-4,0)--Y--X--(-4,10)--cycle); draw((0,-2)--(0,12)--(-2,12)--(-2,8)--B--A--C--(-2,2)--(-2,-2)--cycle); dot(O); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, NW); label(&quot;$O$&quot;, O, NE); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, NW); label(&quot;$W$&quot;,W , NE); label(&quot;$X$&quot;, X, N); label(&quot;$Y$&quot;, Y, S); label(&quot;$Z$&quot;, Z, SE); [/asy]\" width=\"377\" height=\"215\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/0/f4060296f6cfc830dd8eff64c7db0c55e89d49ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{15}4\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{21}4\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{27}4\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{21}2\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{27}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"413\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/3/c53abe86595a36cddb3cc6632040e0e565a7213b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" />, the vertical distance between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the vertical distance between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/3/5a3f8058d992b335e01696b6ca50a49faaac9cbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 5 - 1 - 1 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"160\" height=\"16\" />. We are given that the length of the altitude of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is equal to the distance between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/0/c80824e034824ed29992f2284ddc5342f7afaf76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 1 + \\frac{5}{2} = \\frac{9}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"115\" height=\"38\" />. So the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/3/5830846816adade258c0e98e74136171c789b61c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}\\left(3\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"79\" height=\"45\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/b/ffbdd38cd4e38a68ac90264273b91611360d20b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} \\ \\frac{27}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"69\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~sidkris\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4RBCH1rUcSw\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4RBCH1rUcSw</a>\n</p><p>~David\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8\" title=\"2003 AMC 8\">2003 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2003\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" 